    {
      "id": "claim_44f4405f3bd241e09cc00250e3845d63",
      "statement": "The Worker split exists because a tight non-yielding infinite loop in learner Java (e.g. while(true){}) ran on the iframe main thread wedged the whole tab, stopping even the timeout timer from firing; moving CheerpJ into a Worker keeps the iframe thread responsive so its timer fires and worker.terminate() can hard-kill the runaway code from outside regardless of what it is doing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L102-L121",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3e054965133c8dad1569b519d45120b5bb79957fefb9a748bc10767b9d1b489c:"
