      "id": "claim_504742c61bfc45ae9dd30bd209d87b25",
      "statement": "The sandbox is defense-in-depth against misbehaving submissions, not a security boundary against a local attacker: the code runs in the visitor's own browser under their own OS user, there is no server and no cross-visitor/shared state to protect, and the static check plus sandbox plus timeout only stop runaway or ill-behaved submissions from hanging the tab or misusing browser-reachable APIs.",
